<figure class="r41-pool" data-r41-pool aria-labelledby="r41-pool-title">
 <figcaption id="r41-pool-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Recover the borrower and the blocker separately</figcaption>
 <p class="note">Chosen states from the disposable drill · two pooled connections · no time scale</p>
 <div class="boundary"><p class="boundary-label">Application · connection ownership</p><div class="requests"><div><strong>A</strong><span data-live data-a></span></div><div><strong>B</strong><span data-live data-b></span></div><div><strong>C</strong><span>No connection acquired; no SQL submitted</span></div></div><p class="count" data-live data-count></p></div>
 <div class="boundary server"><p class="boundary-label">PostgreSQL · transaction dependency</p><div class="holder"><strong>Maintenance holder</strong><span data-live data-holder></span></div><p data-live data-chain></p><p data-live data-note></p></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-live data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <div class="controls"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step aria-label="Step"></span><div data-hold class="hold" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>The complete recovery, as text</summary><p>A and B borrow both pooled connections and wait on the same locked product. C expires while waiting to borrow. Cancelling the idle holder leaves its transaction open. Cancelling A stops A's statement; its application rolls back and returns one connection, while B still waits. Terminating the identified holder discards its uncommitted note and frees the lock. B completes its scratch stock decrement and returns its connection. A's fresh retry finds no stock and changes zero rows.</p></details>
</figure>
<script>
 import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
 document.querySelectorAll('[data-r41-pool]').forEach(root=>{
  const texts=[
   ['Owns connection · blocked','Owns connection · blocked','0 available / 2','Idle in transaction · holds P7','A → B → holder','The uncommitted maintenance note is not visible.','Both borrowers wait inside PostgreSQL. C has no borrowed connection, so its acquisition wait has no corresponding query in pg_stat_activity.'],
   ['Owns connection · blocked','Owns connection · blocked','0 available / 2','Cancel sent · transaction still open','A → B → holder','The note and product lock remain part of the open transaction.','Cancelling the idle holder signals a query, but no query is running. Neither borrower is freed. A successful signal return has not established recovery.'],
   ['57014 · rolled back · returned','Owns connection · blocked','1 available / 2','Transaction still open','B → holder','The blocker has not changed.','The application handles A’s cancellation, rolls back the failed transaction and returns its connection. Pool capacity improves, but B remains blocked on the original holder.'],
   ['Connection available','Scratch decrement committed · returned','2 available / 2','Session terminated · transaction aborted','No remaining lock dependency','The uncommitted note was discarded. P7 stock is now 0.','After checking the holder’s PID and backend start, the drill terminates its session. B can proceed and commit. Losing the holder’s unfinished work is part of the intervention’s cost.'],
   ['Fresh retry · zero rows changed','Finished','2 available / 2','Absent','Queue drained','One stock decrement committed; no maintenance note survived.','A’s new attempt rechecks stock, finds none and changes nothing. Connection recovery succeeded, but the business outcome is “no stock”, not a second successful reservation.']
  ];
  const keys=['a','b','count','holder','chain','note','explanation'];
  stepper(root,{steps:()=>texts.length,draw:n=>keys.forEach((key,i)=>{root.querySelector(`[data-${key}]`).textContent=texts[n][i];})});
 });
</script>
